<td id="Sx1.T7.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="Sx1.T7.3.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">83.14</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T7.3.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="Sx1.T7.3.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">8.02</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T7.3.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="Sx1.T7.3.4.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">73.04</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T7.3.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="Sx1.T7.3.4.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">67.35</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T7.3.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="Sx1.T7.3.4.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5.19</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Effect of data augmentation on ZO-FC.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Sx1.SSx6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Augmentations act as input-space regularization that encourages invariances. In continual learning, that regularization reduces representation drift toward the current task and thus mitigates forgetting. On CIFAR100, removing augmentation (keeping only resize/center-crop) yields similar accuracy, and higher forgetting; on ImageNet-R, the accuracy increases slightly with much higher forgetting. This supports that standard augmentation helps ZO-FC stability rather than hurting ZO quality.</p>
</div>
</section>
