<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SSx8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Runtime–Memory Trade-off: </span>
Table <a href="#Sx1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ H. Memory and Computation Cost Analysis ‣ Appendix ‣ More Than Memory Savings: Zeroth-Order Optimization Mitigates Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows the per-epoch training time and corresponding optimization memory cost. ZO methods achieve extreme memory efficiency, but incur increasing compute overhead with higher query budgets, reflecting the cost of additional function queries. Due to optimizer decomposition for different trainable modules, our approach costs slightly longer runtime than ZO. Despite this trade-off, Our approach’s runtime remains manageable to low-resource hardware.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Computation Cost Analysis: </span>
We use FLOPs to measure computation cost. Let <span id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">B</span> be batch size; <span id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">H<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>W</span> the input resolution (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224{\times}224" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>224</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>224</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224{\times}224</annotation></semantics></math>);
<span id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">N</span> the ViT token count (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1+(H/16)(W/16)=197" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>197</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1+(H/16)(W/16)=197</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>224</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>); <span id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span> the hidden width (ViT-B: <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D{=}768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D{=}768</annotation></semantics></math>);
<span id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C</span> the current #classes; <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐋</mi><mi>𝐚</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math> the #blocks with adapters; and <span id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">r</span> the adapter bottleneck (we use <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Denote the ViT backbone forward cost per image as <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{backbone}}(H,W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>backbone</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{backbone}}(H,W)</annotation></semantics></math>.
A bottleneck adapter applies two linear maps per token (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D{\to}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D{\to}r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{\to}D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{\to}D</annotation></semantics></math>), so the adapter overhead per image is</p>
<table id="Sx1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{PET}}\;\approx\;L_{a}\,N\,(2Dr+2rD)\;=\;L_{a}\,N\,(4Dr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>PET</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{PET}}\;\approx\;L_{a}\,N\,(2Dr+2rD)\;=\;L_{a}\,N\,(4Dr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cosine</em> classifier, each forward computes: feature <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>–norm (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 3D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 3D</annotation></semantics></math> ops),
<em id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">weight</em> <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>–norm across <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> classes (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 3CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 3CD</annotation></semantics></math> ops), class dot-products (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 2CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 2CD</annotation></semantics></math>), and a scalar scale <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim C</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="Sx1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{cls}}\;\approx\;(5CD)+3D+C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{cls}}\;\approx\;(5CD)+3D+C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note.</span> In our implementation, feature and weight normalizations are recomputed <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every forward</em>, so the <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3CD</annotation></semantics></math> term in (<a href="#Sx1.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ H. Memory and Computation Cost Analysis ‣ Appendix ‣ More Than Memory Savings: Zeroth-Order Optimization Mitigates Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is paid per forward. If one caches unit-norm weights (or renormalizes once per optimizer step), then the per-forward cost becomes <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2CD)+3D+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2CD)+3D+C</annotation></semantics></math> with an additional <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3CD</annotation></semantics></math> once per step.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The total <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per-image forward</em> FLOPs is</p>
<table id="Sx1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{fwd,img}}\;\approx\;F_{\text{backbone}}(H,W)\;+\;L_{a}N(4Dr)\;+\;\big(5CD+3D+C\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>backbone</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{fwd,img}}\;\approx\;F_{\text{backbone}}(H,W)\;+\;L_{a}N(4Dr)\;+\;\big(5CD+3D+C\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For per-batch multiplicities (FO / ZO / hybrid), We report FLOPs using the standard convention that a backward pass over the trainable subgraph costs <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math>2× the forward pass, so one training step is <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math>3× the forward FLOPs. So let <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{FC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>FC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{FC}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the FC-classifier backward cost in forward-equivalents of the <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">head</em> subgraph (we use <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{FC}}\!\approx\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>FC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{FC}}\!\approx\!2</annotation></semantics></math>), and let <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> be the ZO (SPSA) query budget:</p>
<ul id="Sx1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FO:</span> forwards/batch <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1</annotation></semantics></math>; backward over <em id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">trainable parts</em> (adapters+head). Cost: <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}\;+\;\alpha_{\text{FC}}\,B\,F_{\text{cls}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>FC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}\;+\;\alpha_{\text{FC}}\,B\,F_{\text{cls}}</annotation></semantics></math> plus the adapter backward (captured by the 3<math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> rule below).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ZO on adapters:</span> forwards/batch <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2q{+}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2q{+}1</annotation></semantics></math>; no backward. Cost: <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;(2q{+}1)\,B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;(2q{+}1)\,B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ZO-FC (early epochs):</span> <math id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2q</annotation></semantics></math> ZO forwards on adapters <math id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> one FO forward for the classifier <math id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> one eval forward; and a classifier-only backward. Cost: <math id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;(2q{+}2)\,B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}\;+\;\alpha_{\text{FC}}\,B\,F_{\text{cls}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>FC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;(2q{+}2)\,B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}\;+\;\alpha_{\text{FC}}\,B\,F_{\text{cls}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ZO-FC (late; classifier frozen):</span> same forwards as ZO: <math id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2q{+}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2q{+}1</annotation></semantics></math>. Cost: <math id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;(2q{+}1)\,B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;(2q{+}1)\,B\,F_{\text{fwd,img}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#Sx1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ H. Memory and Computation Cost Analysis ‣ Appendix ‣ More Than Memory Savings: Zeroth-Order Optimization Mitigates Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), the relative <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per-batch</em> overhead vs. FO is</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta F_{\text{ZO}\;\text{vs}\;\text{FO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mtext>ZO</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vs</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FO</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta F_{\text{ZO}\;\text{vs}\;\text{FO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx 2q\cdot B\cdot F_{\text{fwd,img}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx 2q\cdot B\cdot F_{\text{fwd,img}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta F_{\text{ZO-FC(early)}\;\text{vs}\;\text{FO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mtext>ZO-FC(early)</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vs</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FO</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta F_{\text{ZO-FC(early)}\;\text{vs}\;\text{FO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx(2q{+}1)\cdot B\cdot F_{\text{fwd,img}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx(2q{+}1)\cdot B\cdot F_{\text{fwd,img}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta F_{\text{ZO-FC(late)}\;\text{vs}\;\text{FO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mtext>ZO-FC(late)</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vs</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>FO</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta F_{\text{ZO-FC(late)}\;\text{vs}\;\text{FO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx 2q\cdot B\cdot F_{\text{fwd,img}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>fwd,img</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx 2q\cdot B\cdot F_{\text{fwd,img}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remarks.</span> (i) In FO we backprop through the <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">trainable</em> parts (adapters+classifier); the ViT backbone is frozen (no grads) but still incurs one forward per batch.
(ii) For ViT-B/16 at <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>224</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}197" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>197</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}197</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D{=}768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D{=}768</annotation></semantics></math>; the adapter overhead scales linearly with <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and is small for <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{a}{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{a}{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx1.T11" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Per-batch FLOP <em id="Sx1.T11.21" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">breakdown</em> for FO, ZO, and ZO-FC.
<span id="Sx1.T11.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Forward FLOPs / batch</span> are <span id="Sx1.T11.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">measured</span> once with <span id="Sx1.T11.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fvcore</span> and scaled by the number of forwards in each regime (baseline single-forward cost: <math id="Sx1.T11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8.484\times 10^{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8.484</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8.484\times 10^{11}</annotation></semantics></math>).
<span id="Sx1.T11.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Backward FLOPs / batch</span> are <span id="Sx1.T11.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">estimated</span>: FO via the <math id="Sx1.T11.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math> rule; ZO-FC via the analytical head-only term <math id="Sx1.T11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2B\,F_{\text{cls}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2B\,F_{\text{cls}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Sx1.T11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{=}48,\,D{=}768,\,C{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{=}48,\,D{=}768,\,C{=}5</annotation></semantics></math> at the measured epoch.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
