</table></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="Sx1.T11.28" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left ltx_figure_panel"><span id="Sx1.T11.28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Notes: (i) FO backward is estimated via the rule-of-thumb <math id="Sx1.T11.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{total}}\!\approx\!3\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{forward}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.148em">≈</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>forward</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{total}}\!\approx\!3\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{forward}}</annotation></semantics></math> when training adapters+classifier with a frozen backbone.
(ii) ZO-FC early includes a classifier-only FO step; its backward is <math id="Sx1.T11.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2B\,F_{\text{cls}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2B\,F_{\text{cls}}</annotation></semantics></math> and scales linearly with <math id="Sx1.T11.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
(iii) Because this term is tiny relative to ViT forwards, totals for ZO and ZO-FC practically coincide at the same <math id="Sx1.T11.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="Sx1.SSx8.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Computation Cost Measurement: </span>
We use ViT-B/16 at <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>224</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with batch size <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{=}48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{=}48</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">measured</em> forward FLOPs per image (fvcore) is <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1.768\times 10^{10}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">1.768</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1.768\times 10^{10}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so per-batch forward FLOPs is <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{8.484\times 10^{11}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">8.484</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mn>𝟏𝟏</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{8.484\times 10^{11}}</annotation></semantics></math>. FO total is <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">estimated</em> via the common rule
<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FO,total}}\!\approx\!3\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{forward}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>FO,total</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>forward</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FO,total}}\!\approx\!3\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{forward}}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{2.545\times 10^{12}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">2.545</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mn>𝟏𝟐</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{2.545\times 10^{12}}</annotation></semantics></math> per batch.
ZO performs <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2q{+}1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2q{+}1)</annotation></semantics></math> forward evaluations with no backward; at <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q{=}1</annotation></semantics></math> this matches FO’s total, and at <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q{=}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q{=}4</annotation></semantics></math> it is <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="9\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9\times</annotation></semantics></math> the forward-only batch cost, i.e., <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{7.636\times 10^{12}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">7.636</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mn>𝟏𝟐</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{7.636\times 10^{12}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
ZO-FC uses the same ZO forwards and adds a classifier-only backward during early epochs. Given our small <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and a frozen backbone, this extra term (<math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{FC}}\,B\,F_{\text{cls}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>FC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{FC}}\,B\,F_{\text{cls}}</annotation></semantics></math>) is orders of magnitude smaller than a ViT forward, so totals numerically coincide with ZO at the same <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> (both early and late).
This explicitly reports and quantifies the <em id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">additional forward passes</em> required by ZO and how training cost scales with <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.
In practice, parallelizing the <math id="Sx1.SSx8.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2q</annotation></semantics></math> ZO forwards <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> can reduce wall-clock time without changing FLOPs and is compatible with ZO-FC for on-device continual learning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SSx9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">I. CIL Accuracy Trends: ZO-FC vs. FO Methods</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SSx9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To have a good view of the effectiveness of our proposed ZO-FC method, we demonstrate the last accuracy trends across the full task stream on both CIFAR100 and ImageNet-R, under two common incremental learning settings: Inc-10 and Inc-5. Figure <a href="#Sx1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ I. CIL Accuracy Trends: ZO-FC vs. FO Methods ‣ Appendix ‣ More Than Memory Savings: Zeroth-Order Optimization Mitigates Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <a href="#Sx1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ I. CIL Accuracy Trends: ZO-FC vs. FO Methods ‣ Appendix ‣ More Than Memory Savings: Zeroth-Order Optimization Mitigates Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, <a href="#Sx1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ I. CIL Accuracy Trends: ZO-FC vs. FO Methods ‣ Appendix ‣ More Than Memory Savings: Zeroth-Order Optimization Mitigates Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, <a href="#Sx1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ I. CIL Accuracy Trends: ZO-FC vs. FO Methods ‣ Appendix ‣ More Than Memory Savings: Zeroth-Order Optimization Mitigates Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> illustrate the evolution of performance as more tasks are introduced. These trends highlight the long-term stability of ZO-FC under class-incremental learning.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.21019v1/cifar_inc5_overview.png" id="Sx1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/456;" width="685" height="456" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx1.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="Sx1.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CIFAR100, Inc-5: last accuracy over tasks.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.21019v1/inr_inc5_overview.png" id="Sx1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/456;" width="685" height="456" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx1.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="Sx1.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ImageNet-R, Inc-5: last accuracy over tasks.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.21019v1/cifar_inc10_overview.png" id="Sx1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/456;" width="685" height="456" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx1.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="Sx1.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CIFAR100, Inc-10: last accuracy over tasks.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.21019v1/inr_inc10_overview.png" id="Sx1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/456;" width="685" height="456" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx1.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="Sx1.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ImageNet-R, Inc-10: last accuracy over tasks.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
